---
description: Rules for Screen Reader platform adapters (Windows UI Automation, capture, OCR)
globs: packages/reader/src/sidelight_reader/platform/**
alwaysApply: false
---

Follow @docs/design/reader-v0.1.md. In this folder:

- Implement the Protocols in `platform/base.py`; do not change them without updating the design spec.
- Use thin wrappers only: `ctypes` for Win32, `comtypes` for UI Automation, `pywinrt` (`winrt-*`) for Windows.Media.Ocr and Graphics Capture.
- Frame bytes live only in memory and are released right after OCR. No saving frames, even for debugging.
- Import Windows modules lazily so `import sidelight_reader` works on Linux and macOS.
- Tests that touch real Windows APIs get `@pytest.mark.windows`; everything else uses fakes.
